# libblas-dev (Base BLAS Library)
# Provides the standard BLAS API (Basic Linear Algebra Subprograms) for fundamental operations like vector and matrix addition, multiplication, and dot products.
# Other higher-level libraries, like LAPACK and OpenBLAS, depend on BLAS.

# liblapack-dev (Advanced Linear Algebra via LAPACK)
# Built on top of BLAS, LAPACK provides more complex routines like Solving systems of linear equations, Eigenvalue problems, Singular Value Decomposition (SVD).

# libopenblas-dev (Optimized BLAS Implementation)
# A high-performance, optimized implementation of BLAS that can replace the reference BLAS for better efficiency.
# includes both BLAS and LAPACK APIs, so technically it can replace libblas-dev and liblapack-dev in most cases.
# However, Some projects might explicitly depend on libblas-dev or liblapack-dev, Installing all three ensures compatibility with a wide range of software.


